# Certificates got and renewed as they are asked for: an HTTPS server
# that names the hosts it may answer for and a CA's ACME directory, and
# nothing else - Go's golang.org/x/crypto/acme/autocert, over std/acme,
# std/tls and std/http.
#
# HTTP integration uses Server.serve(host, port, config, Handler), where
# Handler.new(config) constructs AutocertView on its own serving task.
# Handler#tls_config exposes only that task's server configuration.
# Copy directory URL, cache path, allowed domains and account settings
# in AutocertConfig; never pass a live view, listener, TLS config or
# mutable ACME session between tasks. HTTP and TLS workers independently
# read challenge answers from the same private cache directory.
#
# Autocert.run(config) runs the manager until Autocert.stop is posted.
# Set config.accept_terms only after accepting the CA's terms, and
# config.email to the account's contact address. The manager and its
# flights remain under the caller's owning task group; cancellation
# joins all flight cleanup before another manager may start.
#
# **A certificate per name, on demand.** `tls_config` is a std/tls server
# config whose `identity_source` is a task-local view: each ClientHello's
# server_name is looked up, and the first handshake for a name with no
# certificate held gets one - from the cache if one there is valid for
# the name and not expired, or by an order from the CA - while the
# handshake waits. One P-256 key and one name per certificate, as Go's
# manager makes them. A client that names no host, or one the host policy
# refuses, is refused (unrecognized_name) before the cache or the CA is
# asked, and one whose certificate could not be had is refused with
# internal_error: config.hosts allows only its configured names, as
# Go's `HostWhitelist` does, each name compared
# as server_name carries it - ASCII, its A-labels for a Unicode one,
# without the trailing dot, in lower case.
#
# **One order at a time for a name.** Handshakes that ask for a name
# while its order runs wait for that order and take what it ends with;
# they do not place their own. An order that fails is remembered for its
# name: the handshakes after it are refused at once with its error until
# `retry_ms` has passed, and twice that after a second failure in a row,
# up to an hour - so a name the CA will not issue for is not asked for on
# every handshake. The manager owns its held map, flight handles and
# retry counts. Each flight owns an independent protocol session and
# challenge cleanup. Handshake tasks see only the Copyable config and
# the cache: no mutable manager fields are reached by TLS callbacks.
#
# **A handshake waits no longer than its deadline.** std/tls tells the
# view what is left of the handshake's time (`HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS`, or
# the server's own), and its wait is cut to that and config.wait_ms.
# The handshake is refused with internal_error then and lets its socket
# go. Its order continues in the manager's group, even if every waiting
# handshake times out. Later handshakes poll the same certificate/error
# files; each has an independent deadline and backoff timer.
#
# Without Autocert.run there is no order service. A cached certificate
# is still usable; a cache miss posts an order and waits only until its
# own deadline. Handshakes never run an inline ACME order. A call to
# certificate outside a handshake waits config.wait_ms at most too.
# A false board post is harmless; subsequent polls retry while time
# remains, and the next handshake can post again.
#
# **Chains checked.** A chain the CA issues is checked by std/x509 for
# the name, to config.roots_pem (system roots when empty), before cached or
# shown, and so is one read from the cache: a chain from any other CA is
# refused (internal_error), not kept.
#
# **Challenges.** config.challenges names those offered in the order
# tried, tls-alpn-01 then http-01 unless set: each a fresh order, the
# next tried when one's authorization fails. tls-alpn-01 (RFC 8737) is
# answered by this same listener: `tls_config` adds `acme-tls/1` to the
# protocols it speaks by ALPN, and a client that offers it alone - the
# CA's validation, nothing else does - is shown the challenge certificate
# for the name while its order runs and refused otherwise; a client that
# offers anything beside it never is. http-01 is answered on port 80 by
# `answer`, from a task-local HTTP handler; dns-01 is not offered, since
# its record goes in a zone this cannot reach.
#
# **Renewal.** Autocert.run, in a task of the caller's group, renews each
# certificate the manager holds config.renew_before_ms (thirty days)
# before it expires - or, for one whose whole life is no longer than
# that, once two thirds of it have passed - with a new key, and publishes
# the new PEM for later handshakes; it retries a failed renewal after
# config.retry_ms, doubling to an hour. Autocert.stop posts the stop
# variant and ends the manager. Servers keep valid cached certificates.
# A view reloads changed PEM even before its own copy's renewal time.
#
# **The cache** (`AutocertCache`) keeps the account key under
# `acme_account+key` and each name's key and chain, as PEM, under the
# name. `AutocertDirCache` is a directory, made 0700 where it is not
# there, each entry written to a file of its own and renamed over the
# old - so a reader sees the old or the new whole - and created 0600:
# certificate entries hold private keys. AutocertCache remains the
# get/put/delete contract; AutocertConfig selects AutocertDirCache so
# independently configured tasks read the same result store.
#
# Not here: ACME Renewal Information (RFC 9773) - renewal is by the
# certificate's dates alone; jitter on the renewal time; RSA certificate
# keys beside ECDSA ones for clients that take no ECDSA; external account
# binding; deactivating an authorization left pending by a failed order;
# revocation; dns-01, and so wildcard names; several names on one
# certificate. Failures are cached until their recorded until_ms.
#
# test/ris/autocert.ri gates completion broadcast, independent deadlines,
# failure expiry, renewal reload, stop and manager isolation with a local
# issuer. autocert_wire.ri gates Copyable config and bounded orders with
# zero heap. Part B updates bench/std_autocert_exercise.sh and its driver
# for Python SSL and Pebble: chain trust, host policy before ordering,
# ten first handshakes making one order, restarts without an order,
# short-lived renewal seen as a new serial before expiry, rejected
# untrusted chains, handshake deadlines, and directory/cache modes.
#
# Certificates on demand, with one process-wide board protocol.
#
# Copy AutocertConfig into Autocert.run(config) in a service task and
# into AutocertView.new(config) in each HTTP/TLS worker. A view supplies
# tls_config and answer; it never reaches the manager's mutable state.
# A second running manager is refused, even for another cache directory.
# Stop by posting Autocert.stop; cached certificates remain available.
#
# Orders carry names or Stop on RisBoard. Completion is broadcast through
# the directory cache, never through replies addressed to a waiter.
# Each handshake polls with its own deadline (50 ms doubling to 500 ms).
# Its timeout leaves the manager's flight running. Failure files contain
# until_ms and the original error; all waiters see it until that time.
#
# Each flight owns its ACME session: mutable clients cannot cross task
# boundaries. Sessions use the same account key, prepared by the manager
# before starting flights. Account registration with that key is idempotent.
# Flight tasks publish whole PEM entries by atomic rename. The manager
# joins completed flights and owns deduplication and renewal scheduling.
# Challenges are cache entries too, removed by flight cleanup.
#
# Views check the cached PEM on every lookup and rebuild their task-local
# identity when it changes. Valid certificates remain usable during a
# renewal or after stop. Chains are checked to config.roots_pem (system
# roots when empty); config.ca_roots_pem sets the ACME HTTPS trust roots.
# Allowed names are normalized as TLS server names before comparison.
# Refused names never touch the cache or the CA.
#
# Renewal keeps the existing policy: thirty days before expiry, or two
# thirds through a shorter life, with retry backoff doubling to an hour.
# The cache retains its 0700 directory, 0600 entries, account key name,
# and certificate PEM format. Additional entries are <name>.error,
# challenge-tls-<name>, challenge-http-<token> and autocert+stats.
# Use a private directory
# for each configuration. Only one manager process may write that cache.
#
# Not implemented: ARI, renewal jitter, RSA certificate keys, external
# account binding, authorization deactivation, revocation, dns-01,
# wildcard names or multiple names per certificate.

module std/autocert

import std/indexable
import std/text

import std/acme::{AcmeClient, AcmeError, AcmeHttp01, AcmeTlsAlpn01, AcmeOrder}
import std/x509::{X509, X509Error, SigningKey, Certificate}
import std/p256::{P256PrivateKey}
import std/ecdsa::{EcdsaError}
import std/file::{File}
import std/dir::{Dir}
import std/tls::{TlsClient, TlsConfig, TlsServerConfig, TlsIdentity, TlsError, TlsAlert}
import std/http::{HTTPClient, Request, Response}
import std/random::{Random}
import std/base64::{Base64}
import std/time::{Time, Span}

# Why a certificate could not be had, or the cache not read or written.
pub struct AutocertError
  getter detail : String

  def initialize(@detail : String)
  end

  def to_s : String
    message
  end
end

impl Error for AutocertError
  def message : String
    "autocert: #{@detail}"
  end
end

# Where a manager keeps its account key and its certificates: text by
# key, nil for a key not held. Every value it is given holds a private
# key.
pub trait AutocertCache
  abstract def get(key : String) : String | AutocertError | Nil
  abstract def put(key : String, data : String) : AutocertError?
  abstract def delete(key : String) : AutocertError?
end

# A cache in a directory: an entry a file named by its key. The directory
# is made, 0700, the first time it is written to where it is not there;
# an entry is written to a file of its own in it, created 0600 (the
# umask may take more away, never less), then renamed over the old one.
pub class AutocertDirCache
  getter dir : String

  def initialize(@dir : String)
  end

  # A key that is a file in the directory and nothing else: no separator,
  # not empty, not `.` or `..`.
  private def path(key : String) : String | AutocertError
    if key.empty? || key == "." || key == ".." || key.includes?("/") || key.includes?("\\")
      return AutocertError.new("#{key.inspect} is not a cache key")
    end
    "#{@dir}/#{key}"
  end
end

impl AutocertCache for AutocertDirCache
  def get(key : String) : String | AutocertError | Nil
    path = path(key)
    return path if path.is_a?(AutocertError)
    return nil unless File.exists?(path)
    AutocertFiles.read(path)
  end

  def put(key : String, data : String) : AutocertError?
    path = path(key)
    return path if path.is_a?(AutocertError)
    AutocertFiles.put(@dir, path, data)
  end

  def delete(key : String) : AutocertError?
    path = path(key)
    return path if path.is_a?(AutocertError)
    return nil unless File.exists?(path)
    # Cleanup cannot spawn a child into an already cancelled group.
    # File deletion is synchronous and owns no parked IO operation.
    if IyiScheduler.current.cancelled
      File.delete(path)
      return nil
    end
    AutocertFiles.delete(path)
  end
end

# File calls answer a failure by panicking; here it is an error value,
# the call run as a task whose panic is read as its answer.
struct AutocertFiles
  @[TaskClosureUnsafe("joins the reader before closing its packed input")]
  def self.read(path : String) : String | AutocertError | Nil
    answer = nil.as(String | AutocertError | Nil)
    image = RisTaskConfig.new(path.as_tape)
    defer image.close
    group do |g|
      task = g.spawn { File.read(image.read(Str).to_heap) }
      got = task.value
      if got.is_a?(Panicked)
        # A concurrent success may retire an error/challenge entry after
        # the caller's exists check. Disappearance is a cache miss.
        answer = File.exists?(path) ? AutocertError.new("reading #{path}: #{got.message}") : nil
      elsif got.is_a?(Cancelled)
        answer = AutocertError.new("reading #{path}: cancelled")
      else
        answer = got
      end
    end
    answer
  end

  @[TaskClosureUnsafe("joins the writer before closing its packed input")]
  def self.put(dir : String, path : String, data : String) : AutocertError?
    image = RisTaskConfig.new({dir.as_tape, path.as_tape, data.as_tape})
    defer image.close
    error = nil.as(AutocertError?)
    group do |g|
      task = g.spawn do
        folder, target, bytes = image.read(Tuple(Str, Str, Str))
        Dir.mkdir_p(folder.to_heap, 0o700) unless Dir.exists?(folder.to_heap)
        temporary = "#{target.to_heap}.#{AutocertPem.hex(Random::Secure.random_bytes(8))}.tmp"
        defer File.delete(temporary) if File.exists?(temporary)
        File.open(temporary, "w", perm: 0o600) { |io| io.write(bytes.to_heap) }
        File.rename(temporary, target.to_heap)
        0
      end
      got = task.value
      error = AutocertError.new("writing #{path}: #{got.message}") if got.is_a?(Panicked)
      error = AutocertError.new("writing #{path}: cancelled") if got.is_a?(Cancelled)
    end
    error
  end

  @[TaskClosureUnsafe("joins cleanup before closing its packed input")]
  def self.delete(path : String) : AutocertError?
    image = RisTaskConfig.new(path.as_tape)
    defer image.close
    error = nil.as(AutocertError?)
    group do |g|
      task = g.spawn do
        input = image.read(Str).to_heap
        File.delete(input) if File.exists?(input)
        0
      end
      got = task.value
      error = AutocertError.new("deleting #{path}: #{got.message}") if got.is_a?(Panicked)
    end
    error
  end
end

# A certificate a manager holds for a name: the identity handshakes are
# shown, its dates, and when renewal is next tried.
pub class AutocertHeld
  getter identity : TlsIdentity
  getter not_before_ms : Int64
  getter not_after_ms : Int64
  # When renewal is next tried: its due time, later after failures.
  property renew_at_ms : Int64
  property failures : Int32 = 0

  def initialize(@identity : TlsIdentity, @renew_at_ms : Int64)
    @not_before_ms = @identity.leaf.not_before.to_unix_ms
    @not_after_ms = @identity.leaf.not_after.to_unix_ms
  end

  # Whether a handshake at *now_ms* may be shown it.
  def current?(now_ms : Int64) : Bool
    now_ms >= @not_before_ms && now_ms < @not_after_ms
  end
end

# Configuration is finite Copyable data, including PEM trust roots.
@[OnTape]
pub struct AutocertConfig
  getter directory_url : Str
  getter cache_dir : Str
  getter hosts : Ary(Str)
  property email : Str = "".as_tape
  property accept_terms : Bool = false
  property wait_ms : Int32 = 60000
  property retry_ms : Int32 = 60000
  property renew_before_ms : Int64 = 2592000000_i64
  property challenges : Ary(Str)
  property roots_pem : Str = "".as_tape
  property ca_roots_pem : Str = "".as_tape

  def initialize(@directory_url : Str, @cache_dir : Str, @hosts : Ary(Str))
    @challenges = Ary(Str).new(2)
    @challenges << "tls-alpn-01".as_tape << "http-01".as_tape
  end

  def allows?(name : String) : Bool
    @hosts.any? { |host| AutocertView.normalize(host.to_heap) == name }
  end
end

pub enum AutocertControl
  Certificate
  Stop
end

@[OnTape]
pub struct AutocertOrder
  getter name : Str
  getter control : AutocertControl

  def initialize(@name : Str, @control : AutocertControl = AutocertControl::Certificate)
  end

  def self.stop : AutocertOrder
    new("".as_tape, AutocertControl::Stop)
  end
end

# A view and its parsed identities belong to exactly one serving task.
@[OnTape]
pub class AutocertView
  ACCOUNT_KEY = "acme_account+key"
  MAX_RETRY_MS = 3600000_i64
  getter config : AutocertConfig
  getter cache : AutocertDirCache
  @held : Hash(String, AutocertHeld) = {} of String => AutocertHeld
  @versions : Hash(String, String) = {} of String => String
  @placeholder : TlsIdentity? = nil

  def initialize(@config : AutocertConfig)
    @cache = AutocertDirCache.new(@config.cache_dir.to_heap)
  end

  def self.normalize(host : String) : String
    name = TlsClient.server_name_for(host)
    name.is_a?(TlsError) ? host : name.downcase
  end

  # A std/tls server config that shows this manager's certificates, and
  # speaks *alpn*'s protocols with `acme-tls/1` after them. Its own
  # `identity` is a self-signed certificate for `autocert.invalid` that
  # no handshake is shown: the manager answers each one itself.
  @[TaskClosureUnsafe("TLS callbacks run on the view owner task before its tape ends")]
  def tls_config(alpn : Array(String) = ["http/1.1"]) : TlsServerConfig
    config = TlsServerConfig.new(placeholder)
    protocols = alpn.dup
    protocols << AcmeTlsAlpn01::PROTOCOL unless protocols.includes?(AcmeTlsAlpn01::PROTOCOL)
    config.alpn = protocols
    config.identity_source = ->(name : String?, offered : Array(String)?, left : Int32?) { identity_for(name, offered, left).as(TlsIdentity | TlsError | Nil) }
    config
  end

  private def placeholder : TlsIdentity
    if held = @placeholder
      return held
    end
    made = AutocertPem.new_key
    now = Time.utc
    # Neither can fail on a key made here and a name that is a host's.
    der = X509.self_signed(SigningKey.new(made.key), ["autocert.invalid"], now - Span.days(1), now + Span.days(3650)).or_panic
    identity = TlsIdentity.from_der([der], made.key).or_panic
    @placeholder = identity
    identity
  end

  def identity_for(server_name : String?, alpn : Array(String) | Ary(String) | Nil, left_ms : Int32? = nil) : TlsIdentity | TlsError
    return TlsError.new("autocert: the client names no host (server_name)", TlsAlert::UNRECOGNIZED_NAME) unless server_name
    name = server_name.downcase
    if alpn && alpn.size == 1 && alpn[0] == AcmeTlsAlpn01::PROTOCOL
      text = @cache.get("challenge-tls-#{name}")
      if text.is_a?(String)
        challenge = TlsIdentity.from_pem(text, text)
        return challenge if challenge.is_a?(TlsIdentity)
      end
      return TlsError.new("autocert: no tls-alpn-01 challenge is up for #{name}", TlsAlert::UNRECOGNIZED_NAME)
    end
    held = certificate(name, left_ms)
    if held.is_a?(AutocertError)
      return TlsError.new(held.message, @config.allows?(name) ? TlsAlert::INTERNAL_ERROR : TlsAlert::UNRECOGNIZED_NAME)
    end
    held.identity
  end

  # A cached identity is local; compare whole PEM to detect every rewrite,
  # including renewals in the same filesystem timestamp tick.
  def certificate(name : String, left_ms : Int32? = nil) : AutocertHeld | AutocertError
    return AutocertError.new("#{name.inspect} is not a name this manager answers for") unless @config.allows?(name)
    limit = @config.wait_ms
    cut = left_ms ? left_ms < limit : false
    limit = left_ms if left_ms && cut
    why = cut ? "left of the handshake's time" : "of wait_ms"
    deadline = Time.monotonic.total_milliseconds.to_i64 + limit
    pause = 50
    waiting = false
    loop do
      return AutocertError.new("the wait for #{name}'s order was cancelled") if IyiScheduler.current.cancelled
      if waiting && Time.monotonic.total_milliseconds.to_i64 >= deadline
        return AutocertError.new("#{name}'s order has not ended in the #{limit} ms #{why}")
      end
      now = AutocertPem.now_ms
      if held = load(name, now)
        return held
      end
      if failure = cached_failure(name, now)
        return failure
      end
      left = deadline - Time.monotonic.total_milliseconds.to_i64
      return AutocertError.new("#{name}'s order has not ended in the #{limit} ms #{why}") if left <= 0
      RisBoard.post(AutocertOrder.new(name.as_tape))
      waiting = true
      sleep(left < pause ? left.to_i32 : pause)
      return AutocertError.new("the wait for #{name}'s order was cancelled") if IyiScheduler.current.cancelled
      pause = pause < 500 ? (pause * 2).clamp(50, 500) : 500
    end
  end

  def cached_failure(name : String, now : Int64) : AutocertError?
    text = @cache.get("#{name}.error")
    return text if text.is_a?(AutocertError)
    return nil unless text.is_a?(String)
    lines = text.split("\n", 2)
    return nil unless lines.size == 2
    until_ms = lines[0].to_i64?
    return nil unless until_ms && now < until_ms
    AutocertError.new(lines[1])
  end

  def remember(name : String, error : AutocertError, until_ms : Int64) : AutocertError?
    @cache.put("#{name}.error", "#{until_ms}\n#{error.detail}")
  end

  def load(name : String, now_ms : Int64) : AutocertHeld?
    text = @cache.get(name)
    return nil unless text.is_a?(String)
    held = @held[name]?
    return held if held && held.current?(now_ms) && @versions[name]? == text
    read = held_of(name, text)
    return nil if read.is_a?(AutocertError) || !read.current?(now_ms)
    @held[name] = read
    @versions[name] = text
    read
  end

  def held_of(name : String, text : String) : AutocertHeld | AutocertError
    identity = TlsIdentity.from_pem(text, text)
    return AutocertError.new("the certificate for #{name}: #{identity.message}") if identity.is_a?(TlsError)
    return AutocertError.new("the certificate issued for #{name} does not name it") unless identity.leaf.matches_host?(name)
    chain = Certificate.from_pem(text)
    return AutocertError.new("the certificate for #{name}: #{chain.message}") if chain.is_a?(X509Error)
    verified = X509.verify(identity.leaf, chain[1, chain.size - 1], trust!, name)
    return AutocertError.new("the certificate for #{name} is not trusted: #{verified.message}") if verified.is_a?(X509Error)
    AutocertHeld.new(identity, renew_time(identity.leaf.not_before.to_unix_ms, identity.leaf.not_after.to_unix_ms))
  end

  # `roots`, or the system's.
  private def trust : Array(Certificate) | AutocertError
    unless @config.roots_pem.empty?
      given = Certificate.from_pem(@config.roots_pem.to_heap)
      return AutocertError.new(given.message) if given.is_a?(X509Error)
      return given
    end
    system = TlsConfig.new.trusted_roots
    return AutocertError.new("the system's roots, which a chain is checked to: #{system.message}") if system.is_a?(TlsError)
    system
  end

  def renew_time(not_before_ms : Int64, not_after_ms : Int64) : Int64
    life = not_after_ms - not_before_ms
    ahead = @config.renew_before_ms
    return not_after_ms - ahead if ahead < life
    not_before_ms + life * 2_i64 // 3_i64
  end

  def backoff(count : Int32) : Int64
    wait = @config.retry_ms.to_i64
    i = 1
    while i < count && wait < MAX_RETRY_MS
      wait = wait * 2_i64
      i = i + 1
    end
    wait < MAX_RETRY_MS ? wait : MAX_RETRY_MS
  end

  # Process counters are cache data too; views never reach manager state.
  def orders : Int32
    statistics(0)
  end

  def renewals : Int32
    statistics(1)
  end

  private def statistics(index : Int32) : Int32
    text = @cache.get("autocert+stats")
    return 0 unless text.is_a?(String)
    fields = text.split("\n")
    index < fields.size ? (fields[index].to_i? || 0) : 0
  end

  def answer(request : Request) : Response?
    path = request.path
    return nil unless path.starts_with?(AcmeHttp01::PATH)
    return Response.new(405, "", {"Allow" => "GET, HEAD"}) unless request.method == "GET" || request.method == "HEAD"
    token = path[AcmeHttp01::PATH.bytesize, path.bytesize - AcmeHttp01::PATH.bytesize]
    text = @cache.get("challenge-http-#{token}")
    return Response.new(404, "") unless text.is_a?(String)
    Response.new(200, text, {"Content-Type" => "application/octet-stream"})
  end

  def add_challenge(name : String, token : String, authorization : String) : AutocertError?
    key = AutocertPem.new_key
    der = AcmeTlsAlpn01.certificate(name, authorization, SigningKey.new(key.key))
    return AutocertError.new(der.message) if der.is_a?(AcmeError)
    text = AutocertPem.key(key) + AutocertPem.pem("CERTIFICATE", der)
    error = @cache.put("challenge-tls-#{name}", text)
    return error if error
    error = @cache.put("challenge-http-#{token}", authorization)
    @cache.delete("challenge-tls-#{name}") if error
    error
  end

  def remove_challenge(name : String, token : String) : Nil
    @cache.delete("challenge-tls-#{name}")
    @cache.delete("challenge-http-#{token}")
  end
end

# Protocol state belongs to this flight alone. Only files cross tasks.
@[OnTape]
pub class AutocertIssuer < AutocertView
  @client : AcmeClient? = nil
  @transport : HTTPClient? = nil

  def issue(name : String) : AutocertError?
    defer close_transport
    made = order(name)
    made.is_a?(AutocertError) ? made : nil
  end

  private def close_transport : Nil
    if transport = @transport
      transport.close
    end
  end

  private def client : AcmeClient | AutocertError
    if made = @client
      return made
    end
    stored = @cache.get(ACCOUNT_KEY)
    return stored if stored.is_a?(AutocertError)
    key = nil.as(SigningKey?)
    if stored
      read = SigningKey.from_pem(stored)
      return AutocertError.new("the account key in the cache: #{read.message}") if read.is_a?(X509Error)
      key = read
    else
      fresh = AutocertPem.new_key
      written = @cache.put(ACCOUNT_KEY, AutocertPem.key(fresh))
      return written if written
      key = SigningKey.new(fresh.key)
    end
    trust = TlsConfig.new
    trust.alpn = ["http/1.1"]
    unless @config.ca_roots_pem.empty?
      roots = Certificate.from_pem(@config.ca_roots_pem.to_heap)
      return AutocertError.new(roots.message) if roots.is_a?(X509Error)
      trust.roots = roots

    end
    transport = HTTPClient.new(idle: 0, tls: trust)
    @transport = transport
    session = AcmeClient.new(@config.directory_url.to_heap, key, http: transport)
    return AutocertError.new("the CA's directory: #{session.message}") if session.is_a?(AcmeError)
    session.wait_ms = @config.wait_ms
    contact = @config.email.empty? ? [] of String : ["mailto:#{@config.email.to_heap}"]
    account = session.register(contact, terms_agreed: @config.accept_terms)
    return AutocertError.new("the account: #{account.message}") if account.is_a?(AcmeError)
    @client = session
    session
  end

  # A new certificate for *name* from the CA, under a new key, put in the
  # cache: an order proved by each of `challenges` in turn - a fresh order
  # for the next only when the last one's authorization failed - and
  # finalized.
  private def order(name : String) : AutocertHeld | AutocertError
    acme = client
    return acme if acme.is_a?(AutocertError)
    failures = [] of String
    @config.challenges.each do |kind|
      placed = acme.new_order([name])
      return AutocertError.new("the order for #{name}: #{placed.message}") if placed.is_a?(AcmeError)
      proved = prove(acme, placed, name, kind.to_heap)
      return finish_order(acme, placed, name) unless proved
      failures << "#{kind.to_heap}: #{proved.message}"
    end
    AutocertError.new("no certificate for #{name}: #{failures.empty? ? "no challenges to offer" : failures.join("; ")}")
  end

  private def prove(acme : AcmeClient, placed : AcmeOrder, name : String, kind : String) : AutocertError?
    placed.authorizations.each do |url|
      proved = authorize(acme, url, name, kind)
      return proved if proved
    end
    nil
  end

  # *placed*, proved, finalized under a new key; the chain read, checked
  # to be for *name* and the key, and put in the cache with the key.
  private def finish_order(acme : AcmeClient, placed : AcmeOrder, name : String) : AutocertHeld | AutocertError
    key = AutocertPem.new_key
    done = acme.finalize(placed, SigningKey.new(key.key))
    return AutocertError.new("the order for #{name}: #{done.message}") if done.is_a?(AcmeError)
    chain = acme.certificate(done)
    return AutocertError.new("the certificate for #{name}: #{chain.message}") if chain.is_a?(AcmeError)
    text = AutocertPem.key(key) + chain
    held = held_of(name, text)
    return held if held.is_a?(AutocertError)
    stored = @cache.put(name, text)
    return stored if stored
    held
  end

  # The authorization at *url* proved by *kind*, unless it is valid
  # already: the answer put up for the CA, and taken down after.
  private def authorize(acme : AcmeClient, url : String, name : String, kind : String) : AutocertError?
    authorization = acme.authorization(url)
    return AutocertError.new(authorization.message) if authorization.is_a?(AcmeError)
    return nil if authorization.status == "valid"
    challenge = authorization.challenge(kind)
    return AutocertError.new(challenge.message) if challenge.is_a?(AcmeError)
    defer remove_challenge(name, challenge.token)
    up = add_challenge(name, challenge.token, acme.key_authorization(challenge.token))
    return up if up
    answered = acme.respond(challenge)
    return AutocertError.new(answered.message) if answered.is_a?(AcmeError)
    valid = acme.wait_authorization(url)
    return AutocertError.new(valid.message) if valid.is_a?(AcmeError)
    nil
  end

end

# The guard is process-wide; it holds no task-owned data.
pub struct Autocert
  @@running = Atomic(Int32).new(0)

  # False means the order bound is full; the caller must retry stop.
  def self.stop : Bool
    RisBoard.post(AutocertOrder.stop)
  end

  def self.run(config : AutocertConfig) : AutocertError?
    run(config, AutocertIssuer)
  end

  # An issuer factory also permits local CA doubles without network IO.
  # F.new(config).issue(name) publishes PEM or returns AutocertError.
  def self.run(config : AutocertConfig, factory : F.class) : AutocertError? forall F
    return AutocertError.new("a manager is already running; one board protocol per process") unless @@running.compare_and_set(0, 1)[1]
    defer @@running.set(0)
    view = AutocertView.new(config)
    if error = view.cache.put("autocert+stats", "0\n0")
      return error
    end
    held = {} of String => AutocertHeld
    flights = {} of String => IyiTask(Int32)
    failures = {} of String => Int32
    orders = 0
    renewals = 0
    images = {} of String => RisTaskConfig
    config.hosts.each do |host|
      name = AutocertView.normalize(host.to_heap)
      if certificate = view.load(name, AutocertPem.now_ms)
        held[name] = certificate
      end
    end
    defer images.each_value { |image| image.close }
    group do |g|
      loop do
        now = AutocertPem.now_ms
        flights.keys.each do |name|
          task = flights[name]
          next unless task.done?
          got = task.value
          flights.delete(name)
          if completed_image = images.delete(name)
            completed_image.close
          end
          if got == 0
            if certificate = view.load(name, now)
              if held.has_key?(name)
                renewals += 1
              else
                orders += 1
              end
              held[name] = certificate
              view.cache.put("autocert+stats", "#{orders}\n#{renewals}")
              failures.delete(name)
              view.cache.delete("#{name}.error")
            end
          else
            count = (failures[name]? || 0) + 1
            failures[name] = count
            until_ms = now + view.backoff(count)
            stored_error = view.cache.get("#{name}.error")
            if stored_error.is_a?(String)
              recorded_until = stored_error.split("\n", 2)[0].to_i64?
              until_ms = recorded_until if recorded_until
            end
            if got.is_a?(Panicked)
              view.remember(name, AutocertError.new(got.message), until_ms)
            end
            if certificate = held[name]?
              certificate.renew_at_ms = until_ms
            end
          end
        end
        wake_at = now + 3600000_i64
        # Completed flights need no mailbox replies: poll retained tasks
        # while there are any, then return to the renewal deadline.
        wake_at = now + 50_i64 unless flights.empty?
        due = nil.as(Str?)
        held.each do |name, certificate|
          next if flights.has_key?(name)
          if certificate.renew_at_ms <= now
            due = name.as_tape
            break
          end
          wake_at = certificate.renew_at_ms if certificate.renew_at_ms < wake_at
        end
        message = due ? AutocertOrder.new(due) : nil
        unless message
          taken = RisBoard.take(AutocertOrder, wake_at - now)
          return nil if taken.is_a?(Cancelled)
          message = taken[0]
        end
        next unless message
        return nil if message.control == AutocertControl::Stop
        name = message.name.to_heap
        next unless config.allows?(name)
        next if flights.has_key?(name)
        next if view.cached_failure(name, now)
        current = held[name]? || view.load(name, now)
        if current
          held[name] = current
          next if current.renew_at_ms > now
        end
        # Prepare one key before concurrent sessions can register it.
        unless view.cache.get(AutocertView::ACCOUNT_KEY)
          error = view.cache.put(AutocertView::ACCOUNT_KEY,
            AutocertPem.key(AutocertPem.new_key))
          return error if error
        end
        flight_name = name.as_tape
        count = (failures[name]? || 0) + 1
        retry_delay = view.backoff(count)
        task, image = start_flight(g, config, flight_name, retry_delay, factory)
        flights[name] = task
        images[name] = image
      end
    end
    nil
  end

  @[TaskClosureUnsafe("run joins flights before closing their packed inputs")]
  private def self.start_flight(g : IyiGroup, config : AutocertConfig,
                               name : Str, retry_delay : Int64,
                               factory : F.class) forall F
    image = RisTaskConfig.new({config, name, retry_delay})
    task = g.spawn do
      # A flight panic belongs to this inner group, never its siblings.
      outcome = group do |own|
        flight = own.spawn do
          settings, flight_name, delay = image.read(Tuple(AutocertConfig, Str, Int64))
          F.new(settings).issue(flight_name.to_heap)
        end
        flight.value
      end
      settings, flight_name, delay = image.read(Tuple(AutocertConfig, Str, Int64))
      flight_error = if outcome.is_a?(Panicked)
        AutocertError.new(outcome.message)
      elsif outcome.is_a?(AutocertError)
        outcome
      else
        nil
      end
      if flight_error
        worker_cache = AutocertDirCache.new(settings.cache_dir.to_heap)
        written = worker_cache.put("#{flight_name.to_heap}.error",
          "#{AutocertPem.now_ms + delay}\n#{flight_error.detail}")
        raise written.message if written
        1
      else
        0
      end
    end
    {task, image}
  end

end

# A P-256 key made here, and the 32 bytes it is, which std/p256 keeps to
# itself and the cache needs.
struct AutocertKey
  getter key : P256PrivateKey
  getter bytes : Array(UInt8)

  def initialize(@key : P256PrivateKey, @bytes : Array(UInt8))
  end
end

# Keys made here and the PEM they are kept as.
struct AutocertPem
  # The DER of a SEC 1 ECPrivateKey (RFC 5915) on P-256 runs to 121 bytes:
  # version 1, the 32-byte key, the curve's OID, and the 65-byte point.
  # Methods, not constants: an Array constant is heap made at start.
  def self.sec1_head : Array(UInt8)
    [0x30_u8, 0x77_u8, 0x02_u8, 0x01_u8, 0x01_u8, 0x04_u8, 0x20_u8]
  end

  def self.sec1_curve : Array(UInt8)
    [0xA0_u8, 0x0A_u8, 0x06_u8, 0x08_u8, 0x2A_u8, 0x86_u8, 0x48_u8, 0xCE_u8, 0x3D_u8, 0x03_u8, 0x01_u8, 0x07_u8,
     0xA1_u8, 0x44_u8, 0x03_u8, 0x42_u8, 0x00_u8]
  end

  # A new P-256 key from the system's entropy; drawn again in the 2^-32
  # chance its bytes are not below the group's order.
  def self.new_key : AutocertKey
    while true
      d = Random::Secure.random_bytes(32)
      key = P256PrivateKey.from_bytes(d)
      return AutocertKey.new(key, d) unless key.is_a?(EcdsaError)
    end
    raise "unreachable"
  end

  # *made* as an EC PRIVATE KEY block.
  def self.key(made : AutocertKey) : String
    point = made.key.public_point
    raise "autocert: a P-256 point of #{point.size} bytes" unless point.size == 65 && made.bytes.size == 32
    pem("EC PRIVATE KEY", sec1_head + made.bytes + sec1_curve + point)
  end

  def self.pem(label : String, der : Array(UInt8)) : String
    body = Base64.encode(String.new(der.size) { |buf| buf.copy_from(der.to_unsafe, der.size) })
    lines = [] of String
    at = 0
    while at < body.bytesize
      lines << body[at, 64 < body.bytesize - at ? 64 : body.bytesize - at]
      at = at + 64
    end
    "-----BEGIN #{label}-----\n#{lines.join("\n")}\n-----END #{label}-----\n"
  end

  def self.hex(data : Array(UInt8)) : String
    data.map { |x| (x < 16_u8 ? "0" : "") + x.to_s(16) }.join("")
  end

  def self.now_ms : Int64
    Time.utc.to_unix_ms
  end
end
